":3799528066,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887ieDKC","user":{"login":"danieldietzler","id":36593685,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NTkzNjg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36593685?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler","html_url":"https://github.com/danieldietzler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T13:08:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T13:08:37Z","body":"> but the way Github handles secrets prevents us from accessing them on PRs\nOh right, sorry. I missed that your branch is on a fork and not the main repo, my bad!\n\nJust tested it and it still doesn't seem to work unfortunately. If there's any debugging I can do on my end please let me know :) \n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3799528066/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3799678789","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990#issuecomment-3799678789","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990","id":3799678789,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887ien9F","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T13:41:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T13:41:41Z","body":"hmm, weird.\n\nIt would be helpful if you can outline your entire test infra with node names, their IPs, groups/tags/users so we can compare that to the policy.\n\nThen on every node as you run them, run `tailscale debug netmap` to get a dump of the netmap and upload that. We are particularly interested in the `PacketFilter` but lets just get all. \n\nThe best for us is a minimal case, so its easier for us to reproduce it. ","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3799678789/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3801245557","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990#issuecomment-3801245557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990","id":3801245557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887ikmd1","user":{"login":"danieldietzler","id":36593685,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NTkzNjg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36593685?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler","html_url":"https://github.com/danieldietzler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T19:03:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T19:13:29Z","body":"Okay, apologies for the delayed reply. I was able to reproduce it with a minimal example on #3044. I got\n- one user `user1`\n- two nodes\n\t- `node1`: `100.64.0.1`, user device, MacOS\n\t- `node2`: `100.64.0.2`, tagged with `tag:admin`, iPadOS\n\nwith the following ACL:\n```json\n{\n  \"groups\": {\n    \"group:admin\": [\"user1@\"]\n  },\n  \"tagOwners\": {\n    \"tag:admin\": [\"group:admin\"]\n  },\n  \"acls\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"accept\",\n      \"src\": [\"group:admin\"],\n      \"dst\": [\"*:*\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"accept\",\n      \"src\": [\"autogroup:member\"],\n      \"dst\": [\"autogroup:self:*\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`node1` cannot reach `node2` at all, with this netmap output: [node1.json](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24866554/node1.json).\n*However*, interestingly `node2` can reach `node1`, which seems unexpected since, afaik, this policy shouldn't allow that. That has me thinking that perhaps some rule is applied/evaluated the wrong way around here. Unfortunately, since it's on an iPad, I don't have a shell to grab that debug output.\n\n\nEdit: looking back at the test in #3026, the only difference I can see is that in my case both devices belong to the same user. In the test they belong to different users. I thought with tagged-devices that would become meaningless anyways, but maybe not?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3801245557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3804006901","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990#issuecomment-3804006901","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990","id":3804006901,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887ivIn1","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T09:09:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T09:09:40Z","body":"@danieldietzler do you have another device to test with? Its the debug of the output devices that gets all the block rules so we need them too.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3804006901/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3804019392","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990#issuecomment-3804019392","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990","id":3804019392,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887ivLrA","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T09:12:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T09:12:36Z","body":"> However, interestingly node2 can reach node1, which seems unexpected since\n\nwhen you say reach, does that mean you can see it? or actively access services on the device?\n\nIt would be visible, because if one access can access the other, both need to see each other, but it would block services so it would not for example be able to access a web server.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3804019392/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3804776805","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990#issuecomment-3804776805","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990","id":3804776805,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887iyEll","user":{"login":"danieldietzler","id":36593685,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NTkzNjg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36593685?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler","html_url":"https://github.com/danieldietzler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T11:55:39Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T11:55:39Z","body":"> do you have another device to test with? Its the debug of the output devices that gets all the block rules so we need them too.\n\nSince I'm not at home right now, not easily at least. I could swap the roles of the devices around though?\n\n> when you say reach, does that mean you can see it? or actively access services on the device?\n\nSorry, yeah, that's my bad. I assumed seeing == accessing it, but that's not the case. `node2` can see `node1`, but it cannot reach it. `node1` can neither see nor reach `node2`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3804776805/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3804949819","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990#issuecomment-3804949819","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990","id":3804949819,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887iyu07","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T12:27:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T12:27:43Z","body":"> Sorry, yeah, that's my bad. I assumed seeing == accessing it, but that's not the case. node2 can see node1, but it cannot reach it. node1 can neither see nor reach node2\n\nDoes this mean that given this information it is working as expected? or are we still missing some information?\n\nAs a base, it is easier to think og the policy as a \"firewall\" it doesnt hide the device, it will block access to services on it. ","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3804949819/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3804991776","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990#issuecomment-3804991776","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990","id":3804991776,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887iy5Eg","user":{"login":"danieldietzler","id":36593685,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NTkzNjg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36593685?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler","html_url":"https://github.com/danieldietzler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danieldietzler/received_events","type":"User","