 it to be able to reach node2 regardless. \n\nYes this is strange. If you remove the `autogroup:self` rule (comment out).\n\n`node1` is owned by `user1@` which is in `group:admin` meaning it should reach `node2` because `src` `group:admin` => `*:*`.\n\nI am trying to understand if the bug is in `autogroup:self` or if there is another bug. ","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3811631784/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3835815318","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990#issuecomment-3835815318","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2990","id":3835815318,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887koeWW","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T15:21:21Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T15:21:21Z","body":"@danieldietzler ive pushed more fixes to the  pr, can y